Calculate everything for each subtree first.(sub[v])
Then calculate the parent edge using parent edge of parent and subtree of parent.(up[v])

Examples:

Problem: Min dist to a white node for each node
Solution: Answer for each subtree is trivial, but we store first and second minimums.
Parent edge is either parent edge of parent + 1, or first/second minimum of parent + 1.

Problem: Sum of path lengths from each vertex
Solution: For each subtree we sum children and add their subtree size
Parent edge has two components: parent edge of parent, and for each path like that we add 1, and children of parent except current child.
up[v] = (up[pr] + (up_size of parent)) + (sub[pr] - (sub[v] + sz[v]) + (sz[pr] - sz[v])) =
= up[pr] + (up_size of pr) + sub[pr] - sub[v] - sz[v] + sz[pr] - sz[v].
up_size of pr and sz[pr] is exactly n, so the final formula is up[pr] + sub[pr] - sub[v] + n - 2 * sz[v]
